`console\n471d014 Outline rev 10: C8 with exact clipped-excess formula (Brief rev 8)\ndb746a5 Outline rev 9: one gene_expression account, strongest-valid-baseline rule, clip as claim C8\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n-# Outline (story-repo, revision 9 (one account of gene_expression; strongest-valid-baseline reading rule; the clip as claim C8, E9; answers idea-review story-repo#8); revision 8 (the gene_expression gain is the package's λ clip; two PPI++ baselines; answers experiment-repo#6); revision 7 (attribution of the gene_expression gain, C3 scoring by bracketed cells, C4 clause refuted at small n; answers idea-review story-repo#7); revision 6 (first results folded in, section 8; headline arm per tier; C3 factor K/(K−1), Brief rev. 7); venue budget applied; answers idea-review #3 in story-repo)\n+# Outline (story-repo, revision 10 (C8 uses the exact clipped-excess formula of Brief rev. 8); revision 9 (one account of gene_expression; strongest-valid-baseline reading rule; the clip as claim C8, E9; answers idea-review story-repo#8); revision 8 (the gene_expression gain is the package's λ clip; two PPI++ baselines; answers experiment-repo#6); revision 7 (attribution of the gene_expression gain, C3 scoring by bracketed cells, C4 clause refuted at small n; answers idea-review story-repo#7); revision 6 (first results folded in, section 8; headline arm per tier; C3 factor K/(K−1), Brief rev. 7); venue budget applied; answers idea-review #3 in story-repo)\n-| C8 | **A condition under which an existing PPI++ interval can be shortened: the λ clip.** The optimal scalar tuning is λ\\* = b·N/M with b = Cov(Y,f)/Var(f); `ppi-python` 0.2.3 clips λ̂ to [0,1], so when λ\\* > 1 (b above about M/N, so b > 1 for N ≫ n) the package interval is wider than the unclipped one. The gain grows with b − 1 and is given by the known variance formula; it is valid only once n is large enough that the unclipped λ̂ is stable. Refuted if, on a synthetic sweep over b, the width gain does not follow the formula, or the gain is absent at b = 1.5 or 2. It is a statement about one implementation, not about the PPI++ method. | E9 synthetic sweep b ∈ {0.8, 1.0, 1.2, 1.5, 2} against the known V formula, n over the grid, N/n as in E3; real sets: b, λ̂ > 1 fraction, ratio vs unclipped (census_income b = 1.38, gene_expression b = 1.15 are the observed cases; the other sets have b < 1) | Fig 6 (gain vs b, synthetic curve with the real sets marked, coverage shown); one paragraph in the text |\n+| C8 | **A condition under which an existing PPI++ interval can be shortened: the λ clip.** The optimal scalar tuning is λ\\* = b·N/M with b = Cov(Y,f)/Var(f); `ppi-python` 0.2.3 clips λ̂ to [0,1], so when λ\\* > 1 (b above about M/N, so b > 1 for N ≫ n) the package interval is wider than the unclipped one. The exact excess of the package over the floor is (1/n − 1/M)·[Δ + (b\\* − c)²·Var(f)], c = clip(b\\*, 0, M/N) (Brief rev. 8), so the extra term over unclipped PPI++ is (1/n − 1/M)(b\\* − c)²Var(f), zero unless b\\* > 1 + n/N (λ pinned at 1) or b\\* < 0 (λ pinned at 0), and computable per dataset and n; it is given by this formula (the gain grows with b\\* − M/N); it is valid only once n is large enough that the unclipped λ̂ is stable. Refuted if, on a synthetic sweep over b (including b\\* < 0), the measured excess does not follow the formula, or the gain is absent at b = 1.5 or 2. It is a statement about one implementation, not about the PPI++ method. | E9 synthetic sweep b ∈ {0.8, 1.0, 1.2, 1.5, 2} against the known V formula, n over the grid, N/n as in E3; real sets: b, λ̂ > 1 fraction, ratio vs unclipped (census_income b = 1.38, gene_expression b = 1.15 are the observed cases; the other sets have b < 1) | Fig 6 (gain vs b, synthetic curve with the real sets marked, coverage shown); one paragraph in the text |\n-- **E9 The clip (C8).** Synthetic sweep over the slope b with the known variance formula: width of the package PPI++ against unclipped PPI++ (same draws) and the formula, with\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "37b46ab4-d671-50d8-b9d3-0db675dd82ff", "at": 1795688973.5749516, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 53860, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "9ec69c2109a36dd1255aa605ab02ff11", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "6c2fe6a8-a3ec-5392-9a37-b9a8abcb9ce7", "at": 1795688973.5775313, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 53861, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "9ec69c2109a36dd1255aa605ab02ff11", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "8b4107c4-a5da-5e48-a4c0-a8f26749d9c9", "at": 1795688973.5799842, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 53862, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "9ec69c2109a36dd1255aa605ab02ff11", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "f6b9b48a-d676-576f-b370-68c6069da6ef", "at": 1795688973.6489484, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 53863, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "9ec69c2109a36dd1255aa605ab02ff11", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "challenge → credential-required", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "credential challenge GET /world/story-repo.wiki.git/info/refs"}, {"id": "02047a0a-25ad-5a21-b93